From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:10:55 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] pal-pacing

A core that reports a rate more than 2 fps from 60 (PAL content on
fceumm, nestopia, snes9x, snes9x2005_plus, Genesis Plus GX and
pcsx_rearmed, about 50 fps) is paced at its own fps. Locked to the
panel, each tick runs the whole frames its owed frame time adds up to
(0 or 1 at 50 fps, so the last frame repeats about one tick in six;
1 or 2 for a later 75 fps core); undriven, it sleeps one content period
a frame. Its sound is resampled from the core's own rate and passes
1:1 per frame. Every core within 2 fps of 60 keeps the 60 Hz present
and the av_rate stretch, which is also the PAL Speed "Panel" choice in
the NES, SNES, Master System, Mega Drive and PlayStation Screen
sections (Config/pal_speed.txt, Native by default).

Prior art, all GPL-3.0: oauramos/omega-zero paces each core at its own
fps (Pace, commit 726cc34); the 2 fps window and the period-based
core_hz follow cloudwithax/unslot
(https://github.com/cloudwithax/unslot/commit/4cf8468); the fractional
frames-owed carry follows nelynes/slotPlus
(https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/0848fcb,
https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/b264635).
